fs22  \plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Zacharie.\plain \f1\fs22 <\plain \f2\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 (141v)\plain \f2\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 Lc\plain \f2\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 1,68\endash 79\plain \f2\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 (Benedictus);\plain \f2\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 (142r)\plain \f2\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Ymnus\plain \f2\i\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 angelicus.\plain \f1\fs22 <\plain \f2\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 Te\plain \f2\charscalex99\expndtw75\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 deum,\plain \f2\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 CPL\plain \f2\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 Nr.\plain \f2\expndtw-30\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 650;\plain \f2\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 (143r)\plain \f2\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Canticum\plain \f2\i\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 sancte\plain \f2\i\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Marie.\plain \f1\fs22 <\plain \f2\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 Lc\plain \f2\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 1,46\endash 55\plain \f2\expndtw15\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 (Magnificat);\plain \f2\expndtw30\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 >\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Canticum\plain \f2\i\expndtw30\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 Symeonis.\plain \f1\fs22 <\plain \f2\expndtw30\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 Lc\plain \f2\expndtw30\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 2,29\endash 32\plain \f2\expndtw30\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 (Nunc\plain \f2\expndtw30\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 dimittis).\plain \f2\expndtw30\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 Stegm\u252 \'fcller\plain \f2\expndtw30\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 RB\plain \f2\charscalex99\expndtw60\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 Nr.\plain \f2\expndtw-30\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\fs22 21g\endash h. Anl\u228 \'e4sse an den R\u228 \'e4ndern von sp\u228 \'e4terer Hand (16. Jh.).}

